/-!
# A Boolean support checker for the caller domain (LT11, fields 8 and 9)

`allCaller P = true` says that every wire of every instruction of `P`
(including both correction lists of every measurement) is a caller-domain
label: `base i` with `i < 2314`, or one of the four scalar labels
`base 2400, 2409, 2410, 2411`.  It is a plain structural recursion with
`Nat` comparisons, so `decide +kernel` evaluates it on a concrete program.

`allCaller_sound` turns it into `wires P ⊆ callerDomain`, the support premise
`EntrySupportD` / `ExitSupportD` of field 8 (and, by `placed_of_caller`, the
placed-domain premise of field 9).

The structural rules (`allCaller_append`, `allCaller_rename`) and the
`PreservesCaller` facts for the wrapper renamings (`phaseHost`,
`Prefix1590.borrow`, `HostOB5.hostSwap`, the parity swap, `OB5.sig i`) let a
kernel be checked component by component.
-/

